# Project Standards

## Documentation

- **Do not create `.md` / Markdown files** (README, docs, RULE.md, etc.) unless the user explicitly asks for them.

## Modularity (required)

- Prefer **small, focused files**. Split by feature, layer, or responsibility.
- Avoid large single files; extract to modules, helpers, or separate files when it improves clarity.
- Use a **consistent, layered file structure** (e.g. feature folders, core vs features, data/presentation/domain).
- Keep **one main concern per file**; if a file grows beyond ~200–300 lines, consider splitting.

## Code quality

- Prefer **clear naming**, **single responsibility**, and **explicit dependencies**.
- Avoid **premature abstraction**; extract when duplication or complexity justifies it.
- Design so that **structure and patterns do not slow down the app or system**; avoid unnecessary work per frame or per request.
